00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:07.649
Film Courage: In what ways can a writer improve their
dialogue? Daniel Calvisi:  Listening practice, I mean just

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:14.129
keep writing keep rewriting have actors
read it out loud I mean they don't have

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:19.140
to be professional actors but just you
and a friend read it out loud listen to

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.170
how it flows I think that can be really
helpful

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:30.500
I like that listening where are we
listening listening to how people talk

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:37.559
listening to interesting people around
how they talk and then once you write

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:42.120
your dialogue read it out loud you know
do a table read with friends or your

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:49.230
writers group or just even if you read
it out loud yourself find it interesting

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:54.420
that a lot of times people certain
people end their sentences with right or

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.769
you know like and they they continually
do that is that important because even

